---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
import MapStructureDemo from "../../components/MapStructureDemo.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import { lwwMapTerm } from "../../lib/atlas/standalone-terms";
import "../../styles/set-lesson.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="LWWMap" description="Each Eagle Creek map key has its own timestamped conflict rule." territory="Structures" sheetTitle="LWWMap">
  <article class="register-lesson">
    <header class="page-intro"><p class="territory-label">Structures</p><h1>LWWMap</h1><p class="structure-summary">Alice and Bob still have a gate-status line in their notebooks. This time they date each note: the ranger's delivery order does not decide which answer stays.</p><LessonIllustration id="structures-lww-map" /></header>
    <StructureFacts structure="LWWMap" family="CRDT" model="Per-key last-writer-wins map" updates="Write or cross out a text entry" merge="Use the latest time; at equal time, removal wins, then writer ID breaks a tie between writes." delivery="Safe under repeated and out-of-order delivery" bestFor="Offline string settings with a trusted clock policy" cost="Time and writer for each answer or removal" />
    <section aria-labelledby="clock-title"><h2 id="clock-title">A date beside each line</h2><p>An <dfn><a href="/glossary/#lwwmap">LWWMap</a></dfn> compares the time on notes for each named line separately. A note with a later time wins even if another arrives after it. If two notes have the same time, a crossed-out line wins over a new answer; if both contain answers, the writer ID breaks the tie.</p><TermCallout {...lwwMapTerm} /></section>
    <MapStructureDemo kind="lww-map" title="Compare dated gate-status notes" description="Alice and Bob write on the same line. Each notebook uses the time beside that line, not the order in which notes arrive." rule="Use the latest time; if tied, removal wins, then writer ID." raceLabel="Race the dated gate-status notes" />
    <section aria-labelledby="clock-risk-title"><h2 id="clock-risk-title">"Last" depends on the clock</h2><p>A fast watch can make an earlier note win over a later one. Each notebook must keep a crossed-out line until it is safe to forget the removal. Use this rule when one answer is worth that cost.</p></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="source-title">
      <h2 id="source-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Sources:</strong> Watershed's{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/lww_map_kernel.gleam">LWWMap kernel</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Implementation:</strong> The demo calls Watershed through the Gleam toolkit
        for the three-client demo. The runtime issues the clocks compared
        for each key.
      </p>
    </section>
    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through map structures"><a href="/structures/shared-map/">Back to SharedMap</a><a href="/structures/maps/">Browse map family</a><a href="/structures/or-map/">Continue to OR-map</a></nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
